course: dictionary
lesson: 1631
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Chicken» can name a farm bird, the meat we eat, or a feeling of being scared. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: In «Check: 40 legs and 10 chickens with 20 legs», the numbers and legs show that chickens are the animals you count. In «A girl in Leeds ate chicken», the word ate tells you chicken is food.
explain: Slang works the same way. If someone says «Don't chicken out!», the words around it show they are asking you not to be too scared to do something. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Chicken can mean a farm bird that lays eggs.
fact: Chicken can also mean the meat of this bird, which people eat.
fact: In slang, «chicken» means scared, and to «chicken out» means to be too scared to do something.
fact: «A chicken egg takes about 21 days to hatch if kept warm.»
fact: Chickens come from the red junglefowl of southern China and South-East Asia.
exercise: «Check: 40 legs and 10 chickens with 20 legs.» Each chicken has 2 legs. How many legs do 10 chickens have? | 10 | 12 | 40 | *20
exercise: Lily says, «Don't chicken out!» What does chicken out mean? | To cook a meal for the family | *To be too scared to do something | To lay an egg
exercise: «A chicken egg takes about 21 days to hatch if kept warm.» How many days is that? | 100 | *21 | 7 | 2
test: «Foxes hunt chickens because they are hungry.» What does hunt mean here? | *To chase and catch for food | To lay eggs in a nest | To sing loudly in the morning | To sleep under a tree
test: Someone asks, «Which came first, the chicken or the egg?» What kind of question is this? | *A puzzle with no easy answer | A recipe for making soup | A rule about how to look after a farm
exam: «A girl in Leeds ate chicken that had been left out all day and was sick for two days.» What does this teach you about chicken as food? | Chicken is safe to eat at any time | Chicken should always be kept on the counter | *Chicken left out too long can make you ill | Chicken is a kind of fish
